    <statement><p>Write the following decimals as percentages.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 2.33 = }</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 0.233 = }</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 0.0233 = }</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>233.00\%</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>23.30\%</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2.33\%</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>To change a decimal to a percentage, we move the decimal point to the right twice.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 2.33 = 233\% }</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 0.233 = 23.3\% }</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 0.0233 = 2.33\% }</m></p>
</solution>
